          "name": "Mikołaj Bojańczyk"
        },
        {
          "name": "Aristotle (Harmonic)"
        }
      ],
      "bibEntries": []
    },
    "abstract": "Part A of the book *Transducers* (M. Bojańczyk), together with the definitions of its introduction: continuous string-to-string functions, Mealy machines, their closure under composition, continuity and decidable equivalence, the Krohn–Rhodes decomposition theorem into reversible and flip-flop machines, map lifting, and the characterisation of aperiodic Mealy machines as compositions of flip-flops.\n"
  },
